ation."}]}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, a student targeting Industrial Chemist should be able to say:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I can perform and document chemical and instrumental analyses, interpret laboratory results, follow industrial quality and safety procedures, investigate deviations and abnormal results, understand chemical manufacturing processes, analyse laboratory data using statistical and digital tools, and contribute to quality control and process optimisation.”"},{"type":"h","text":"Best career strategy"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Applied Sciences / Industrial Chemistry","Laboratory/QC Internship","QC Chemist / Laboratory Chemist","Industrial/Analytical Chemist","Specialise in Analytical Chemistry, Process Chemistry, Quality or R&D","Technical Specialist / Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"For long-term career growth, the strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Industrial Chemistry","Analytical Instrumentation","Quality Systems","Process Understanding","Data Analytics","AI/Automation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This keeps the graduate employable in conventional chemical industries while also preparing for digital laboratories, automated quality control, sustainable chemistry and AI-assisted industrial R&D."}]}]}